```

The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
imx6_set_lpm(WAIT_UNCLOCKED);
cpu_do_idle();
```
Reason:
The CPU sets 'WAIT_UNCLOCKED' and enters the idle state, which stops the local timer. If another CPU enters the 'WFI' state instead of 'WAIT', the local timer interrupt does not fire, preventing the CPU from waking up at the expected time.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (++num_idle_cpus == num_online_cpus())
    imx6_set_lpm(WAIT_UNCLOCKED);
if (num_idle_cpus-- == num_online_cpus())
    imx6_set_lpm(WAIT_CLOCKED);
```
Reason:
The fix ensures that the CPU transitions to 'WAIT_CLOCKED' when all CPUs are idle, allowing the local timer to remain active and ensuring that the CPU can wake up at the expected time, even if another CPU enters the 'WFI' state.

